  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.6: Security and assurance update for the encrypted path (signed-token wire format unchanged). SECURITY: the validator now pins AES-GCM parameters to the v1 profile — a full 16-byte (128-bit) tag and 12-byte nonce — and rejects any other length; previously the tag length was taken from the token, so a truncated tag could downgrade authentication strength and make tokens malleable. SECURITY: strict, canonical base64url decoding (RFC 7515 §2) rejects embedded whitespace and non-canonical slack bits, so token strings are non-malleable. Both issues were surfaced by a new adversarial fuzz suite (PqJwtFuzzTests). Added executable security invariants (SecurityInvariantsTests), a model-checked TLA+ model of the validator (docs/formal), and a BenchmarkDotNet suite. Tokens produced by this library's builder are unaffected by the stricter decoding. Production-oriented preview: NOT independently audited, NOT a drop-in OAuth/OIDC/JWT replacement. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
